NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114536","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114536","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114536.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114536.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Looking at `get_cell_tile_data()`, I found that it calls `get_cell_source_id()`, `get_cell_atlas_coords()`, and `get_cell_alternative_tile()` separately, each of which does its own `tile_map_layer_data.find()`. That's three hashmaps for what could be done with one.\r\n\r\nProbably not a big deal, but this method gets called a lot when working with tilemaps, so it might seemed worth cleaning up\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\n- Replaced the three separate getter calls with a single `find()` lookup\r\n- Access the cell data directly from the iterator instead of going through the individual getters","closed_by":{"login":"kellemar","id":350990,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MDk5MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/350990?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kellemar","html_url":"https://github.com/kellemar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kellemar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kellemar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kellemar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kellemar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kellemar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kellemar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kellemar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kellemar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kellemar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issu